The browser page public/index.html is the client component Browser page (DSN-003, REQ-004 REQ-007 REQ-008 REQ-002 REQ-001 REQ-005 REQ-009 REQ-010). The first line in <head> of public/index.html is <!-- @trace DSN-003 REQ-004 REQ-007 REQ-008 REQ-002 REQ-001 REQ-005 REQ-009 REQ-010 -->.

Declaration shapes of the changed and added classes, to match exactly; the constructor parameters are fixed:
Task (DSN-005):
export interface Task {
  id: string;
  text: string;
  done: boolean;
  createdAt: number;
  dueDate: string | null;
}

TaskController (DSN-006):
export class TaskController {
  constructor(private readonly taskService: TaskService);
  page(): Promise<string>;
  list(today: string | undefined): Promise<TaskView[]>;
  create(body: { text: string; dueDate?: string | null; }): Promise<Task>;
  update(id: string, body: { text?: string; done?: boolean; dueDate?: string | null; }): Promise<Task>;
  remove(id: string): Promise<void>;
}

TaskService (DSN-007):
export class TaskService {
  constructor(private readonly taskStore: TaskStore);
  list(today: string | undefined): Promise<TaskView[]>;
  isOverdue(task: Task, today: string): boolean;
  add(text: string, dueDate: string | null): Promise<Task>;
  setDone(id: string, done: boolean): Promise<Task>;
  editText(id: string, text: string, dueDate: string | null | undefined): Promise<Task>;
  remove(id: string): Promise<void>;
  normalizeText(text: string): string;
  normalizeDueDate(dueDate: string | null): string | null;
}

TaskStore (DSN-008):
export class TaskStore {
  constructor(db: DatabaseSync);
  findAll(): Promise<Task[]>;
  findById(id: string): Promise<Task | null>;
  insert(task: Task): Promise<void>;
  update(task: Task): Promise<void>;
  delete(id: string): Promise<void>;
}

TaskView (DSN-009):
export interface TaskView extends Task {
  overdue: boolean;
}

Patch only the files these IDs involve, then run typecheck and detect_drift and fix until both are clean.
